Checked at Tau Ceti f790474. The declarations exist as cited:
- NumberField.NarrowClassGroup.mem_closure_of_sq_eq_one (Quadratic/Conjugation/Ambiguous/Narrow.lean:268; 'this needs no hypothesis on the signature of K');
- TauCeti.Multiquadratic.genusCharFunElementaryTwoQuotientFamilyLinearMap_injective (Multiquadratic/Quadratic/GenusCharacter/PrincipalGenus.lean:112; 'Equivalently, the #s genus characters span the full dual of Cl⁺(K)/Cl⁺(K)²');
- mem_range_genusCharFunElementaryTwoQuotientFamilyLinearMap_iff (:79; the image is the sum-zero hyperplane);
- narrowTwoRank_eq_ncard_ramifiedPrimes_sub_one (Quadratic/TwoRank.lean:243);
- NumberField.card_ker_toClassGroup_le_two (Quadratic/Conjugation/NarrowClassGroup.lean:172).
The reviewed audit rates Multiquadratic Layer 2 built ('in the narrow class group, for either signature') and Layer 3 built ('the 2-rank formula … for the narrow class group, either signature'). The paper uses both surjections without proof (p. 80, 'Genus theory gives natural surjections'), with Cl the narrow class group. For x ∈ 𝒟 the ramified primes are exactly the p_i, and the prime discriminants are the p_i, with 8 when 2 | x (χ₈ = χ₂). So item 227's note, which calls Layers 2–3 plans, is wrong. Item 5's note is also wrong to list 'the kernel of Cl⁺ → Cl has order at most 2' as a missing step. Medium is right: a design would re-plan genus theory that is built.
The fix overstates, though, because neither surjection is stated in the paper's form.
- The first needs [Up(p_i)]² = 1 in Cl⁺ (NumberField.NarrowClassGroup.mk0_sq_eq_one_of_map_ringOfIntegersQuadraticConj_eq_self, Narrow.lean:203) and the step from generation to the surjection 𝔽₂^r → Cl⁺[2].
- The second is the transpose of the injective family map. It needs the paper's Galois characters χ_{p_i} identified with the library's ideal-theoretic genus characters. The built Artin bridge TauCeti.Multiquadratic.autCandidateGenusFieldEquivNarrowElementaryTwoQuotient_artinHomAway (CandidateGenusField/Relative/Artin.lean:345) supplies that identification, but no declaration states the composite.
By the standard of finding 1, item 227 keeps status planned at Multiquadratic Layers 2–3, and its note is rewritten. The note says the layers are built, cites these declarations, and lists the remaining glue: the square of Up(p_i), generation to surjection, duality, the Galois-to-ideal identification and the prime-discriminant indexing. The alternative is to restate the item in the library's form (Cl⁺[2] is generated by the classes of the ramified primes; the genus characters separate Cl⁺/Cl⁺²), mark it library, and keep the paper's two maps in the note. Item 5 cites tauceti:NumberField.card_ker_toClassGroup_le_two as proposed. It stays missing because of finding 5.

Checked. The twelve prerequisites include none of Rédei [38, 39], Rédei–Reichardt [40], Heilbronn [23], MacWilliams [34], Watkins [46, 47] or Jutila, and each is the source of routed items:
- (7.27), credited on p. 75 to 'classical work of Rédei' (item 210);
- Rédei reciprocity, which Theorem 3.2 generalizes (pp. 1, 4; item 80);
- Heilbronn, on p. 92 and after (8.44) (items 249, 250 and 261);
- MacWilliams, on pp. 74 and 82 (items 207 and 230);
- Watkins [46], on pp. 61, 71 and 74 (items 184, 187, 200 and 206), and [47] on p. 76;
- Jutila (finding 3).
No atlas packet reads any of them. The ArithmeticStatistics MacWilliams node cites later restatements and says 'MacWilliams 1969 itself remains unread'. Crossref (30 September 2026) confirms the proposed data and gives the DOIs: 10.1515/crll.1934.170.69 (Rédei–Reichardt), 10.1515/crll.1934.171.131 and 10.1515/crll.1939.180.1 (Rédei), 10.4153/CJM-1973-090-3 (Heilbronn), 10.1080/00029890.1969.12000160 (MacWilliams) and 10.4064/aa-27-1-191-198 (Jutila). Watkins's notes have no DOI. Low is right.
Adjustments:
- Give each Rédei work its own 'why'. Only [40] is behind (7.27); [39] is the source of Rédei symbols and reciprocity (item 80); [38] is cited only in the history on p. 2 and is optional.
- List both Watkins notes with their URLs: [46] for the effective A in Propositions 7.6 and 7.8 and for Theorem 7.10, and [47] for the effective m = 2 case (finding 10).
- The note [46] now served is the version of 18 July 2021, later than the paper's retrieval on 19 April 2021, and the entry should say so.
For the fixer: the paper's [38] prints its year as 1935, but Crossref and zbMATH give 1934. It may be recorded as a misprint affecting nothing, like E51.
